WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.479
“The calm before the storm.”

00:00:02.479 --> 00:00:07.350
As a metaphor, it normally means a lull that
occurs just before a huge and often catastrophic

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.940
event takes place.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.429
However, there is such a thing as a literal
calm before a storm.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:18.270
The saying comes from a weather phenomenon
where a tranquil period of stillness and serenity

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:24.511
takes place, only for the winds to start picking
up, the rain to start falling, and the storm

00:00:24.511 --> 00:00:27.400
to suddenly begin to hammer down.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.870
Nobody likes being caught outside when a thunderstorm
rolls into town, but thunder isn’t always

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.940
the worst part of a storm.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.230
That sudden and unsettling flash of lightning
that unpredictably cracks across a dark sky

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:46.470
- the electricity - erratic and volatile in
behavior - might just be the part that startles

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:53.060
you into wishing - hoping - praying to return
to the calm before the storm.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.360
SCP-938 is an entity composed of sheer electrical
energy.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.110
Forget the notion of a simple dynamic current
with an unassuming physical form, and imagine

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:08.580
more - a creature composed of pure relentless
electricity.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.900
Far from just a benign and passive phenomenon,
SCP-938 is considered a formidable and menacing

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.460
predator by the SCP Foundation.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.360
What kind of prey could a being made out of
electricity be interested in hunting?

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.590
Well, that’s easy: power grids.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:29.740
During moderate electrical storms, SCP-938
will appear, traveling through the static

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.740
electricity carried by such storms.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:39.010
Lightning strikes are a form of static electricity,
and when they are expelled, SCP-938 uses these

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.070
strikes to attack its prey.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.930
So, picture it, a stormy night, the rumble
of thunder overhead.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.200
Every booming sound is accompanied by a bright
flash, maybe even a forked strike of lightning

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.520
that appears for a brief second.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.270
And carried within that lightning is SCP-938,
hurling through the sky towards its target:

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.760
the nearest electrical grid.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:08.340
Now, at this time, it is unknown whether or
not SCP-938 actually actively causes electrical

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.229
storms to occur.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:15.459
Research into the weather patterns in the
areas the entity has appeared has proven inconclusive,

00:02:15.459 --> 00:02:19.790
and there is no proof that this power-based
predator is able to influence the weather.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:25.970
However, the second that SCP-938, as a lightning
strike, makes contact with the nearest power

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.440
grid, the surrounding area normally suffers
a complete loss of all power.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.800
Street lamps will go out, plunging the entire
city or town into total darkness.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.390
This doesn’t last forever though, as you
might expect.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:43.709
You see, this creature has the potential energy
of a storm, much like the ones it uses to

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:44.709
travel.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:50.810
SCP-938 isn’t out to absorb more energy
from national or local power grids - or at

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.190
least, certainly not all at once.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.069
What the entity actually does is the following.

00:02:56.069 --> 00:03:01.410
After the brief loss of power, SCP-938 will
quietly infiltrate an electrical grid that

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:07.129
provides energy to a town, city, state, or
even an entire country.

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:12.370
From within, the entity then chooses a structure,
seemingly at random, to monitor.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:17.709
These are usually occupied buildings like
homes, offices, or apartment complexes, with

00:03:17.709 --> 00:03:18.930
plenty of people inside.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:24.300
And no, it doesn’t then delight in turning
on its charge and frying all those inhabitants,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.830
transforming the building into a giant bug
zapper.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.740
But the more people in a structure, the more
electrical appliances and devices you’re

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.790
likely to find inside.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.909
SCP-938 stays dormant for a while, hiding
out in the power grid and is usually only

00:03:38.909 --> 00:03:43.560
detectable by special equipment designed to
monitor electromagnetic fields.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.720
However, the next time a storm comes a-rolling
into town, the living electrical energy wakes

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.300
up and begins to cause havoc.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:56.390
The easiest-to-spot indicator of this is that
SCP-938 will normally begin interfering with

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.159
any electrical devices in the structure it
has chosen.

00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:04.110
Its goal is to cause enough disruption that
it draws the attention of the inhabitants

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.420
living there.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.450
People inside this building will quickly realize
that their appliances aren’t working as

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:14.019
they should be, sparking and malfunctioning
to an alarming degree.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:18.799
These devices will then even cause severe
electrocutions to any who come into direct

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:20.949
physical contact with them.

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:26.300
In every case, this increased electrical activity
has caused the neural impulses of anyone in

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.580
the chosen building to be shut down, resulting
in death.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.770
There are only two instances where this didn’t
happen.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:40.009
In 1987, during an incursion with SCP-938,
two victims had their hearts stopped after

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:43.240
being electrocuted by devices affected by
the entity.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.759
Fortunately, these two individuals survived
after being successfully resuscitated but

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:51.509
suffered long-term psychological damage as
a result of the incident.

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:56.669
Both were noted to have lost significant portions
of their memories and even had their mannerisms

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:59.449
and personalities dramatically altered.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:05.331
After a storm, SCP-938 will return to the
atmosphere, once again in the form of a lightning

00:05:05.331 --> 00:05:09.600
strike, and free from the power grid it was
previously hiding in.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:15.789
From that point, the entity will aim to repeat
the process all over again, in a new location,

00:05:15.789 --> 00:05:20.160
fixating on a new building and claiming the
lives of more innocent civilians.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.139
However, this is not a set-in-stone pattern
of behavior for SCP-938.

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:29.879
Analysis of the electromagnetic field readings
taken in the creature’s vicinity show that

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:35.710
it is at least somewhat capable of the same
level of conscious thought as most human beings,

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:40.669
displaying similar electrical fluctuations
to the neural activity of a human brain.

00:05:40.669 --> 00:05:46.800
Perhaps it is through this disembodied capacity
for thought that SCP-938 occasionally chooses

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.210
a specific person to pursue.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:54.099
Although it is unclear what criteria the electrical
entity looks for in a target, the creature

00:05:54.099 --> 00:05:59.949
has been known to fixate on a single individual
and track them for an extended period of time.

00:05:59.949 --> 00:06:06.259
In one instance, SCP-938 pursued a target
for thirty-six years, eleven months, and six

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:10.360
days until that person died of natural causes.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.749
These targets, designated as SCP-938-A, will
experience symptoms similar to those suffered

00:06:16.749 --> 00:06:22.159
by individuals suffering from various stress
or paranoia-related psychological disorders.

00:06:22.159 --> 00:06:27.190
This includes the rapid onset of conditions
like post-traumatic stress disorder and paranoid

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.749
schizophrenia.

00:06:28.749 --> 00:06:34.710
SCP-938-A instances will also quickly develop
severe phobias, even if they have never exhibited

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:35.990
these previously.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:41.749
However, these aren’t what SCP-938 looks
for in a victim, instead these disorders and

00:06:41.749 --> 00:06:46.680
conditions seem to be directly caused by the
influence of the entity itself.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.830
But the side effects of being in the vicinity
of SCP-938 don’t stop there.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:55.500
In fact, some of the SCP Foundation’s own
personnel have even been affected.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.869
According to several members of Theta 9, a
Mobile Task Force codenamed ‘Bad Moon Rising’,

00:07:00.869 --> 00:07:05.629
being close enough to the entity can trigger
subtle yet unsettling hallucinations.

00:07:05.629 --> 00:07:10.629
The most common of these is the sight of a
cluster of eyes that glow with iridescent

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:15.740
colors, meaning they appear to change shade
when viewed from different angles.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.419
Reportedly appearing in poorly lit areas,
these eyes seem to watch a person that is

00:07:20.419 --> 00:07:22.360
suffering from this hallucination.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:26.389
The iridescent eyes have been seen in the
shadows of other people, as well as appearing

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:29.770
in dense foliage like bushes or hedgerows.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:35.240
Even after the Foundation was able to successfully
contain SCP-938, staff reported that these

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.719
hallucinations still continued to persist.

00:07:37.719 --> 00:07:43.300
But while on the topic of containment, you’re
probably wondering: How does the SCP Foundation

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.589
manage to keep a being of pure electricity
secure?

00:07:46.589 --> 00:07:49.679
Well, with great difficulty is the short answer.

00:07:49.679 --> 00:07:54.449
They actually spent almost half a century
trying to contain SCP-938.

00:07:54.449 --> 00:07:56.229
Why did it take them so long?

00:07:56.229 --> 00:08:02.689
In part, that was down to the wildly unpredictable
nature of SCP-938 and how it moves using electrical

00:08:02.689 --> 00:08:03.689
storms.

00:08:03.689 --> 00:08:08.550
Sure, predicting exactly when and where a
storm is going to hit isn’t impossible,

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:13.159
just tricky to achieve with pinpoint accuracy
- especially if you’re deciding in advance

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:16.349
which day to go to the beach or have a picnic
in the park.

00:08:16.349 --> 00:08:21.340
But even if you knew beforehand that a storm
was on its way to an area, there is no indicator

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:24.339
that SCP-938 would be coming with it.

00:08:24.339 --> 00:08:26.800
They’re squirrely little anomalies like
that.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:32.519
Another factor preventing the Foundation from
containing SCP-938 was a simple case of poor

00:08:32.519 --> 00:08:33.519
timing.

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:38.659
When they first encountered the entity, it
was still 1943; A time when they didn’t

00:08:38.659 --> 00:08:43.089
even have close to the sufficient technological
advancement required to track and contain

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:44.089
the creature.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:48.720
The entity was, after all, made from a tremendous
amount of electrical energy, more than could

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.480
be safely stored in any one device or location
with the tech available in 1943.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:09:00.101
All the Foundation could hope to do was mitigate
the threat that SCP-938 posed, focusing on

00:09:00.101 --> 00:09:02.920
trying to predict its movement and behavior.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:06.860
For a while, containment just seemed like
it wasn’t an option.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:11.790
Six years later, the first instance of SCP-938-A
appeared.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:16.230
This was the person that we mentioned earlier,
who the electric energy entity followed for

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.500
almost thirty-seven years.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:24.140
In this case, the Foundation’s security
personnel were able to get to SCP-938-A first,

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.940
and kept them out of the grasp of the predatory,
power-based creature.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:32.779
These security forces soon became part of
Mobile Task Force Theta 9, and they took charge

00:09:32.779 --> 00:09:36.790
of ensuring SCP-938-A remained safe.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:42.410
And for a while, they achieved this, until
the target died of a heart attack in 1986.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:47.090
You already know that part, but what you don’t
know is that ten minutes before the target’s

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.629
death, an ambulance arrived at the Foundation’s
safe house.

00:09:50.629 --> 00:09:55.089
No member of Bad Moon Rising had called the
emergency services, and the local dispatch

00:09:55.089 --> 00:09:58.350
center hadn’t even received a call for assistance
to that safe house.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:03.750
The emergency dispatcher on duty that night
had spotted an unanswered request for an ambulance

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.329
on his computer terminal.

00:10:05.329 --> 00:10:10.520
It’s almost as if something had interfered
with the machine, in order to lure the ambulance

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:16.240
into responding to SCP-938-A.
This is what prompted the Foundation to once

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:20.240
again consider the possibility of containing
SCP-938.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:26.320
They knew it would be an expensive endeavor,
this was 1989 after all, but as soon as a

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:32.720
possible new SCP-938-A target had been identified,
the Foundation had the perfect bait to catch

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.459
the creature that had eluded them since the
1940s.

00:10:36.459 --> 00:10:41.899
Luring it in with its new target, SCP-938
was successfully captured and contained within

00:10:41.899 --> 00:10:44.529
a Capacitor Bank at a Foundation research
site.

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:49.790
A Capacitor Bank is a series of electrical
capacitors, joined and kept parallel with

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.110
each other, for the purposes of storing electrical
energy.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:57.750
Think of it as a big battery, except there
is a key difference between the two.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:02.379
While batteries store electrical energy as
some form of chemical energy like lithium,

00:11:02.379 --> 00:11:08.279
a capacitor is, in basic terms, designed to
store pure electrical energy.

00:11:08.279 --> 00:11:12.180
Exactly like what SCP-938 is made from.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:16.640
Containment wasn’t without its teething
problems, however, and SCP-938 almost made

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.129
an escape in 1991.

00:11:19.129 --> 00:11:24.209
Bio-Containment and Research Site 06 suffered
a ‘Silent Night’ breach scenario, and

00:11:24.209 --> 00:11:28.949
SCP-938 was able to cause considerable damage
to the site’s infrastructure.

00:11:28.949 --> 00:11:34.310
The building itself was left completely unsalvageable,
and the Capacitor Bank for storing the entity

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:38.439
had to be rebuilt before SCP-938 was recaptured.

00:11:38.439 --> 00:11:44.399
The new Capacitor Bank was moved to Bio-Containment
and Research Site 07, and kept in a fully

00:11:44.399 --> 00:11:46.730
electrically insulated storage warehouse.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:51.370
The entire structure was built to have no
wiring or electrical systems of any kind,

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:55.389
with no metal supports in the concrete it
was constructed from.

00:11:55.389 --> 00:12:00.290
Even staff with pacemakers or metal prosthetics
aren’t allowed inside.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:06.089
There is nothing conductive, nothing metal,
nothing electrical: in short, there is no

00:12:06.089 --> 00:12:09.389
way SCP-938 could ever escape again.

00:12:09.389 --> 00:12:14.649
Hopefully, at least, just as long as no one
brings anything electronic into Storage Warehouse

00:12:14.649 --> 00:12:15.649
Zero.

00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:21.121
Unfortunately, on December 21st 2005, a Foundation
doctor entered the warehouse as part of a

00:12:21.121 --> 00:12:24.380
routine inspection of the creature’s ongoing
containment.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.440
What this doctor had clumsily forgotten was
that he had been carrying a USB flash drive

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:32.860
on his person, and didn’t realize his mistake
until the next day.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:37.149
After he recognized his error, he submitted
the memory stick for examination, only to

00:12:37.149 --> 00:12:41.709
find that everything stored on it had been
wiped, replaced with indecipherable, meaningless

00:12:41.709 --> 00:12:42.709
data.

00:12:42.709 --> 00:12:47.269
All we can really do is just hope that data
is all that was on that flash drive.

00:12:47.269 --> 00:12:52.689
After all, surely SCP-938 wasn’t able to
breach its containment again, and escape hidden

00:12:52.689 --> 00:12:55.220
on a USB stick, right?

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:58.700
Perhaps it’s best to play it safe, just
in case.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:02.699
Next time there’s a thunderstorm in your
town, maybe leave home and go for a drive

00:13:02.699 --> 00:13:04.680
somewhere far away for a while.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:09.120
The last thing you’d want is something lurking
throughout the wires in your house, waiting

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.370
and ready to strike.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:16.610
Now go check out “SCP-3999 - I Am At The
Center of Everything That Happens To Me”

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:22.110
and “SCP-5031 - Yet Another Murder Monster”
for more mysterious anomalous entities from

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:22.899
the SCP Foundation!

